cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "turbidity-sensor"
type: software
abstract: >-
  A low-cost turbidity sensor and its software. The sensing element is the bare board from a
  TST-10-type probe, the one on DFRobot's SEN0189 module, in a printed case round a clear tube, read
  by an Arduino Nano. Paired with a syringe that draws culture through the tube on a timer, it follows
  the density of a culture in a vessel that is already running. The repository holds the printed
  cases, a portable C library that models and calibrates the head, the Nano firmware, the sampler's
  logger, and the bench and column data.
keywords:
  - turbidity
  - optical density
  - photobioreactor
  - microalgae
  - open hardware
  - arduino
authors:
  - family-names: "Brooks"
    given-names: "Cameron"
version: "0.5.0"
url: "https://github.com/uwo-fast/turbidity-sensor"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uwo-fast/turbidity-sensor"
